/ A member a program adds lands on the nearest thing that lives on (decision 564): a variable's own value keeps it,
/ but a plain value inside another value (the number under %d.t%) has nowhere to keep one. That write is an error
/ under its own key — never a silent success, never a crash.
Start
- set %d% = {"t": 5}
- set %d.t.name% = "x", on error set %key% = %!error.key%
- assert %key% equals "CannotSetChild"
